senses.gloss:
kisara,
(1) adj. and subst. (= Pali kasira, Skt. kṛcchra), difficulty, only in akisara-lābhin and alpakisareṇa, qq.v. The use of the former, beside akṛcchra-l˚, proves that the two forms were not felt as identical. In Pali also (Geiger 〔59.2〕) kicchena kasirena are used together, and evidently taken as ‘different words’. Pkt. only kiccha; our kisara (perhaps influenced by Pali-Pkt. kisa = kṛśa) has no recorded parallel in MIndic;
(2) m. or nt., ‘eine Art wohlriechender Stoff’: Kalpanāmaṇḍitikā, Lüders, Kl. Skt. Texte 2, 〔43〕.
